  "result": "Excellent! All 198 tests pass, including 13 new terms tests. Here's what was implemented:\n\n**src/errors.js**\n- Added `TERMS_INVALID`: \"Terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM.\"\n\n**src/invoices.js**\n- Added `calculateDueDate(issueDate, terms)` helper that:\n  - NET14: issue date + 14 days\n  - NET30: issue date + 30 days (default)\n  - EOM: last day of the month containing the issue date\n  \n- Updated `createInvoice()` to:\n  - Accept optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n  - Validate terms (rejects invalid values with TERMS_INVALID)\n  - Calculate and set `dueDate` based on terms\n  - Include both `terms` and `dueDate` on the invoice\n\n**Tests (13 total)**\n- Default and explicit term handling\n- All three term types (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n- Edge cases: last day of month, leap years, month/year boundaries\n- Integration with discounts and multiple lines\n\nThe due date calculation correctly handles:\n- February in leap (2024) and non-leap (2025) years\n- Year boundaries (Dec 15 + NET30 = Jan 14 of next year)\n- EOM calculations across all months\n\nAll 198 tests pass (185 previous + 13 new).",
